  "text": "term Relative frequency The proportion of observations falling into a given class. For example, if a bag of 55 M & M's has 11 green M&M's, then the frequency of green M&M's is 11 and the relative frequency is 11/55 = 0.20. Relative frequencies are often used in histograms , pie charts , and bar graphs .",
